{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/292275-conspiracy-concept-the-undertakers","id":292275,"title":"Conspiracy Concept: The Undertakers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T11:48:32-07:00","id":292275,"title":"Conspiracy Concept: The Undertakers","content":"<b>History</b><br /> <br /> To cross the line of death is something that should be permanent and irreversible. The Undertakers know this concept is false. Too many monsters defy what should be the natural end of all things. What's worse is some of them spread this concept to other things. The Undertakers are a conspiracy that has existed in one form or another for as long as funeral customs have been practiced by mankind, with members often either having had an occupation related with death or dealing with the bodies of such. By tradition, the first organization of their ilk though took place in the plague ravaged streets of Athens, Greece. They were all collectors of the dead, ill fated souls who had the distasteful job of picking up and removing the diseased corpses of those who had died from the streets and homes of the people, and disposing of them. The trouble was, sometimes a corpse would get back up. <br /> <br /> These Risen souls were usually harmless, but they attracted the Shades of those who could not pay for the ferry across the Styx. Sometimes these Risen would go insane, the Shades manipulating them into doing deeds too perverse to imagine. While little record of the meeting remains, it was agreed upon that the Risen were not the true threat - just a symptom. Instead, the Shades must be targeted. One of the members of this first meeting known only as the Pilgrim, a business man who had lost his entire family and most of his fortune to the ravages of the disease, emptied the rest of his savings into a desperate trip to the Oracle at Delphi to ask her advice on fighting the shades. <br /> <br /> Her answer was frustratingly vague, and unhelpful. &quot;The Dead alone know the secrets of the Dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pilgrim would learn his answer after being ambushed by a group of bandits, left for dead, and experiencing what in modern medical terms would be a Near Death Experience. <br /> <br /> Hades beckoned to his soul, but Charon had denied him entry - and no Geist could take someone who wasn't dead. But, the Ferryman listened to the pleas of the desperate Pilgrim, and gave him what the Oracle had promised - the secrets of the dead. As the Pilgrim was cast back into his body, this knowledge changed him. And when he returned, he replicated his experience with those who were as desperate as he. <br /> <br /> This pattern and story were repeated throughout much of the world - a Psychopomp denying death to one desperate enough to wish its secrets. Man by man, it slowly spread around. Though the patterns might be different from Chapter to Chapter of Undertaker, the fact remains the same. The Shade's powers are now theirs.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b><br /> <br /> The basic fact of requirement to entry in the Undertakers is that the prospective recruit have at some point nearly died, and suffered a near death experience. Sometimes, these are artifically induced by a chapter, but the basic fact remains the same; the Shadeshands only work with someone who in some way has probed the line between life and death. <br /> <br /> With this in mind, the Underkeepers are more decentralized than most other conspiracies. The fact that they even can be called a conspiracy relates more to the endowment than to any large scale organization - it took the rise of the Victorian era and modern telecommunications to really begin to allow Chapters, or local organizations of Underkeepers, to connect with each other on a global scale. As ill - connected as they are, they still have managed to evade both purges from humanity and the monsters, primarily from infiltrating the human organizations that would hide them the best. Many of their members come from the 'Unclean' castes or the priesthood.<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> <br /> Priority number one of any Undertaker cell is to deal with Ghosts and Spirits. While compared to the average cell, they have far more of an advantage over these incoporeal opponents, the knowledge they have of them is limited at best. Dealing with Anchors and the like is obvious enough, but spirits have and likely always will be a headache to categorize for them. Head Undertakers speculate they have something to do with the Risen and Ghostwalkers, but this factor is complicated by the sheer variety of forms and powers a Spirit often can display. <br /> <br /> A secondary concern is Vampires; as an obvious perversion of the line they swear to keep clear, Kindred are an opponent that the Undertakers take very seriously. The Shadeshands allows them to compete in some ways with these opponents, but in the end an Undertaker is just as likely to bring out a cross and a stake as burn them away with ghostly fire. Strix are however, an enemy both the Undertakers and Kindred have formed uneasy alliances against for practical and philisophical reasons. A human rising from the grave to drink the blood of the living is far easier to empithize with than a bird of shadow that takes corpses. <br /> <br /> Ghostwalkers are where the Conspiracy tends to differ on how to deal with. Certain Cells and chapters will pursue Ghostwalkers with a vengance and loathing matching the most zealous Witch-Hunters, while others will consider them natural allies or even potential members. The difference between a Sin-Eater and an Undertaker comes more from which one crossed the line of death. As such, of any Conspiracy, the Undertakers know the most about the Ghostwalkers. The contract between the Geist and Sin-Eater is eerily similar to the Pilgrim's Secrets, and for some Undertakers, but there for the grace of god would they be. <br /> <br /> <b>Endowment</b><br /> <br /> The Shadeshands<br /> <br /> For every dot in this endowment, the Hunter may take a dot in a Numina possessed by a ghost. This endowment can be taken multiple times, for different Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:58:47-07:00","id":292301,"title":"","content":"It's interesting Conspiracy, I must admit. I have nothing to bit-, nitpick about, so just short reply like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T13:20:23-08:00","id":301466,"title":"","content":"That's a sweet name bruh bruh. A lot of potential for new tactics and stuff if you could be bothered with that type of thing. You could stand to elaborate more though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3309-electrick","name":"electrick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T22:14:26-08:00","id":302996,"title":"","content":"Okay, what do the undertakers do for Essence? Spend willpower? Take damage? Buy essence as an endowment? <br /> <br /> Whatever you decide, I hope it's evocative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:48:37-08:00","id":303707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/292275-conspiracy-concept-the-undertakers?p=302996#post302996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay, what do the undertakers do for Essence? Spend willpower? Take damage? Buy essence as an endowment?<br /> <br /> Whatever you decide, I hope it's evocative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think they'd take damage - one bashing/lethal for each essence used. I'd need to go through the numina and probably shake a few things around but the basic concept is they're spending life to tap into death. <br /> <br /> Maybe have a thing where you can take Agg for automatic successes for a numina?<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking of reworking the endowment to focus on two seperate paths - Pilgrim's Secrets (Numina), and Last Rites. You pick one or the other. Last rites represents the more human take and side of life after death, something similar to what Sin-Eaters do in their rituals but with less efficiency/power overall, but would allow you to put spirits to rest etc. etc; Basically a quasibenediction/ritual. Pilgrim's Secrets taps into the unnatural side of life after death and is really efficient in it's a tit for tat exchange of health for power. <br /> <br /> This make sense? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T23:41:29-08:00","id":304229,"title":"","content":"Yes, that would make sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh while you could certainly do your own thing, I just thought I'd mention that there is a merit in the book of deceived that gives people access to essence and some ghost numina.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to adapt it you might make it something like &quot;Touch of the grave endowment: the hunter gains an essence pool of stamina plus their touch of the grave rating, which allows them to purchase the following ghost numina: blah blah blah, for 15 exp points each (if using the first ed rules).&quot; Perhaps they could regain essence by sacrificing health levels.<br /> <br /> No biggie if you don't want to use it, but I thought I should in case you would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-08-2014, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:26:23-08:00","id":313928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/292275-conspiracy-concept-the-undertakers?p=304229#post304229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that would make sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh while you could certainly do your own thing, I just thought I'd mention that there is a merit in the book of deceived that gives people access to essence and some ghost numina.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to adapt it you might make it something like &quot;Touch of the grave endowment: the hunter gains an essence pool of stamina plus their touch of the grave rating, which allows them to purchase the following ghost numina: blah blah blah, for 15 exp points each (if using the first ed rules).&quot; Perhaps they could regain essence by sacrificing health levels.<br /> <br /> No biggie if you don't want to use it, but I thought I should in case you would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late reply but that's pretty interesting. I might look into that. It might be interesting to have a conspiracy sort of fractured into three parts by their endowments. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}